Finding: the fresh-per-iteration cache records 17,253 HITS and only 963 produces per cold pass —
the bench fixture builds every turn from the same template strings (thinking/prompt/answer/
readOutput/bashOutput/grepOutput/oldBlock/newBlock/written), so 18,216 source occurrences collapse
to 963 unique (94.7% duplicates). The pre-cache code re-rendered every occurrence; the cache dedups
within the pass. The -36% cold delta is REAL product behavior (dedup), fixture-amplified in share.
match_only_ms=0.16 is the round-12 Entry-cache reuse path (second call on the same instance skips
rendering AND matching), not a match-only decomposition.
Consequences (v2): bench comments corrected (semantics-preservation claim was wrong for duplicates);
pin corpus gained a byte-identical duplicate source + occurrence/entryID assertions; product doc
gained the within-pass dedup note. Probe binaries/patches kept here; never used for adoption.
